  "tags": ["semantic-coherence", "token-fragments", "noise", "interpretability"]
}

{
  "title": "End-of-text / sentence-boundary detector",
  "explanation": "Both features mark document- or sentence-final signals. The Group feature is almost exclusively activated by the special <|endoftext|> token (a very pure end-of-document detector), while the Baseline feature responds to sentence-/document-final punctuation and closing tokens (periods, quotes, newlines and other terminal tokens). The high Jaccard similarity indicates they implement the same boundary signal, with the group model isolating the explicit special token and the baseline spreading activation over common terminal punctuation and formatting tokens.",
