  "title": "Feature detecting attribute punctuation in reference markup (token '=\"')",
  "explanation": "Both features strongly activate on the punctuation pattern '=\"' that appears in attribute-style reference markup (e.g., {ref-type **=\"** fig} or (#F6){ref-type **=\"** fig}). The Group-SAE snippets skew toward figure references and inline fig captions, while the Baseline-SAE examples include more table references, supplementary/footnote markers, and other ref-type variants. Overall the feature appears to encode a tokenizer/markup boundary (equals plus quote) used across different reference tags rather than semantic content about figures vs tables.",
