}

{
  "title": "Overlap in topical signals but different lexical focus",
  "explanation": "Both features encode a shared topical core (e.g., credit, withdrawal, army, AGN) — reflected in the high Jaccard — but they diverge in what else they pick up. The Group-SAE feature skews toward scientific/abstract nouns and topical concepts (graphene, gauge, surface, tree, reasoning), whereas the Baseline-SAE favors concrete artifacts and lexical/form variants (camera, screw(s), radiant, puzzles, orthographic fragments like ‘ades’). This suggests Group-SAE emphasizes semantic/topic clustering while Baseline-SAE also captures more surface/lexical morphology and concrete object tokens.",
